WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.016 --> 00:00:06.982
Journal Entry: November 22, 1876, London Van Helsing, Arthur, and Jack Seward spent the following afternoon reviewing

2
00:00:06.983 --> 00:00:16.950
the professor’s collection of vampire books, looking for something that could help us hunt down the

3
00:00:16.951 --> 00:00:26.204
count. I continued to watch over Mina; she was weak, pale, and rapidly losing blood─the same symptoms

4
00:00:26.205 --> 00:00:31.688
that Lucy had suffered from before her death. Oh, my beautiful Mina was changing into a vampire!

5
00:00:31.689 --> 00:00:35.928
What were we going to do? "I’ve got it!" The professor said, leaping up from his seat.

6
00:00:35.929 --> 00:00:38.229
"Look here in this old volume. It says that anyone who has fed from a vampire

7
00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:49.484
is destined to change into one themselves . . . unless that master vampire can be killed

8
00:00:49.485 --> 00:00:52.714
before the transformation is completed." The count! We had to kill the count! Without pause, we gathered

9
00:00:52.715 --> 00:00:59.905
our tools and set out for his house; however, it was already too late. All his

10
00:00:59.906 --> 00:01:03.816
belongings had been removed and the windows were boarded up. Sure enough, when we went into the

11
00:01:03.817 --> 00:01:12.562
cellar, we found that all the coffins were gone; only some soil remained scattered on the ground.

12
00:01:12.563 --> 00:01:15.396
My heart sank in my chest. Just then, the sound of a ship’s horn from the harbor

13
00:01:15.397 --> 00:01:19.689
gave me an idea. "What if we’ve scared him off and he’s decided to return to

14
00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:24.634
his castle in Transylvania?" "Quick then!" said the professor. "Let’s get to the docks before he goes

15
00:01:24.635 --> 00:01:26.999
aboard that ship!" We ran as fast as we could to the docks, but alas, the ship

16
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.237
had already set sail. A young cargo loader who noticed that we seemed troubled rushed over

17
00:01:30.238 --> 00:01:35.864
to offer his assistance. "Were you supposed to be on that ship?" he enquired. "No . .

18
00:01:35.865 --> 00:01:41.181
. But, do you know if a tall man dressed in black was on board?" I replied,

19
00:01:41.182 --> 00:01:44.562
catching my breath. "Yes. Actually, it was quite strange," he explained. "He arrived at the last

20
00:01:44.563 --> 00:01:51.895
moment with a long wooden box filled with soil. He demanded that we let him on board.

21
00:01:51.896 --> 00:01:56.268
He paid in cash, so the captain said it was all right." "That’s him!" cried the professor.

22
00:01:56.269 --> 00:02:00.908
"Where is that ship headed?" "Varna, Russia. It’s just a bulky cargo ship, so it’ll take a

23
00:02:00.909 --> 00:02:07.114
couple of weeks to arrive at its destination. There’s a faster ship leaving tomorrow morning at

24
00:02:07.115 --> 00:02:11.487
nine. If you want to catch up with him, I would suggest taking that one." The four

25
00:02:11.488 --> 00:02:18.733
of us agreed that we would take the boat the next morning, which gave us enough time

26
00:02:18.734 --> 00:02:21.931
to return to our homes, pack our suitcases, and prepare ourselves for what lay ahead. Nothing

27
00:02:21.932 --> 00:02:25.860
was going to prevent us from catching that fiend and saving my poor Mina’s life. The next

28
00:02:25.861 --> 00:02:36.241
morning, we set sail for the Black Sea, ready to hunt down Count Dracula once and for

29
00:02:36.242 --> 00:02:41.209
all. After a miserable week on the boat, we arrived at Varna, a few days before the

30
00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:47.295
count’s ship was scheduled to dock. We found a hotel where we could store our suitcases

31
00:02:47.296 --> 00:02:54.211
and each take a warm bath. Then, we waited impatiently for the master vampire’s ship to arrive.

32
00:02:54.646 --> 00:03:00.200
Some days later, we received news that the count’s ship had been rerouted to a nearby town

33
00:03:00.201 --> 00:03:04.798
called Galatz. Had he killed the crew as he’d done on the ship that brought him

34
00:03:04.799 --> 00:03:11.520
to England? Maybe he had cursed them, forcing the captain to change his destination. Whatever the cause,

35
00:03:11.521 --> 00:03:15.711
we were frantic. The professor booked us seats on the next train bound for Galatz, and we

36
00:03:15.712 --> 00:03:20.322
quickly packed our things, anxious to check out of the hotel. We boarded the train at noon

37
00:03:20.323 --> 00:03:22.840
and, several hours later, arrived in Galatz to discover yet another setback. Someone had already come

38
00:03:22.841 --> 00:03:30.594
for the box, and the count was nowhere to be found. "We must hurry," said Van Helsing.

39
00:03:30.595 --> 00:03:37.573
"If we don’t find him soon, Mina will change into a vampire forever!" Our only solution was

40
00:03:37.574 --> 00:03:42.327
to hire a coach and travel to Castle Dracula, but I was terrified at the prospect.

41
00:03:42.328 --> 00:03:49.069
My memories of being held prisoner in that dark castle made me shiver with fright, raising the

42
00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:56.089
hair on the back of my neck. I swallowed hard and admitted to my friends, "I can’t

43
00:03:56.090 --> 00:04:03.192
do it!" "But you must!" begged Arthur. "Without you, we are only three and the count could

44
00:04:03.193 --> 00:04:07.705
defend himself!" I thought for several moments about my beautiful Mina─her fair complexion, her lovely eyes,

45
00:04:07.706 --> 00:04:14.621
and lustrous hair. And then, in my vision, I saw her teeth grow sharp and her face

46
00:04:14.622 --> 00:04:21.945
harden with anger. I recoiled in horror at the thought. "I’ll do it," I finally replied. "I

47
00:04:21.946 --> 00:04:29.958
will face Count Dracula and I will do the deed myself." Our coach thundered toward the

48
00:04:29.959 --> 00:04:32.640
small town of Bistritz at the foot of the mountains, where we stopped to rest before continuing.

49
00:04:32.641 --> 00:04:36.799
We planned to approach the castle after sunrise the next morning to ensure that the count would

50
00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:43.312
be asleep in his casket when we arrived. That gave us enough time to find a

51
00:04:43.313 --> 00:04:50.955
room at the quaint little inn and get some sleep ourselves. When we awoke, we discovered that

52
00:04:50.956 --> 00:04:56.603
the innkeeper had prepared a breakfast for us, and laid out four gold crosses. "Take these," he

53
00:04:56.604 --> 00:05:03.538
said. "We townspeople know why you’ve come back and wish you luck. Be careful." Then, Jack Seward,

54
00:05:03.539 --> 00:05:05.498
Professor Van Helsing, Arthur, and I, Jonathan Harker, climbed back into the coach and made our

55
00:05:05.499 --> 00:05:10.220
way up the steep winding road to the castle. Just before high noon, we pulled up at

56
00:05:10.221 --> 00:05:20.629
the large wooden door of the castle and hopped out of the coach with our bags and

57
00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:29.247
tools, ready to attack. We each carried a gold cross and wore a garlic necklace to

58
00:05:29.248 --> 00:05:34.684
help weaken the count. The professor carried a sharp stake and hammer in a burlap bag. "It’s

59
00:05:34.685 --> 00:05:39.436
this way," I whispered and motioned them to follow me to the back of the castle, where

60
00:05:39.437 --> 00:05:48.777
I knew we’d find the secret double door leading to the coffin room. "I’m pretty sure we’ll

61
00:05:48.778 --> 00:05:51.404
find him down here." We cautiously unlatched the bolts of the door and opened it, letting

62
00:05:51.405 --> 00:05:58.594
rays of sunlight into the cool, dirty room. "There he is!" I pointed. "That is his casket

63
00:05:58.595 --> 00:06:00.841
by the staircase. If we work quietly, we can lift off the lid without disturbing him and

64
00:06:00.842 --> 00:06:03.563
stake him without a struggle." Together, we opened the casket, revealing the body of the count

65
00:06:03.564 --> 00:06:09.602
lying there peacefully with his arms crossed over his chest. As the others stood in a circle

66
00:06:09.603 --> 00:06:16.816
around the casket, holding up their crosses for protection, the professor untied his bag and handed me

67
00:06:16.967 --> 00:06:26.283
the hammer and stake. All of a sudden, the count shifted in his casket, his eyes fluttered

68
00:06:26.284 --> 00:06:33.924
open, and he saw us standing there in a circle around him. Panicked, he sat upright,

69
00:06:33.925 --> 00:06:39.233
baring his sharp, white teeth and lunged toward me. I stumbled backward, and, dropping the stake on

70
00:06:39.234 --> 00:06:46.567
the floor, I grabbed the gold cross from my pocket, thrusting in his face. He recoiled as

71
00:06:46.568 --> 00:06:52.763
though it pained him to set eyes upon it. Then, he turned to face my friends.

72
00:06:52.764 --> 00:06:58.271
Bravely, we all took one step toward him, holding up our crosses close to his face. He

73
00:06:58.272 --> 00:07:03.522
growled in frustration and pushed the doctor and Arthur aside with his strong arms. He was heading

74
00:07:03.523 --> 00:07:06.625
for the door, trying to make an escape! I quickly reached down and picked up the

75
00:07:06.626 --> 00:07:13.046
stake with one hand, tightening my grip on the hammer in my other. I hurried to get

76
00:07:13.047 --> 00:07:15.921
him before he could run away. But then something incredible happened. I guess our attack had left

77
00:07:15.922 --> 00:07:18.310
the count confused, because without realizing it was daytime, he rushed toward the open door, and when

78
00:07:18.413 --> 00:07:29.689
the rays of sunlight struck his face, he dropped to his knees with pain. I decided

79
00:07:29.690 --> 00:07:32.217
to seize the opportunity. I ran to him, looking him square in the eye before I pointed

80
00:07:32.218 --> 00:07:41.430
the stake at his chest, and brought the hammer down hard against it, driving it straight into

81
00:07:41.431 --> 00:07:47.065
his heart. "AAAaaaaahhhh!" he screamed as his eyes flashed the fiery color of hell. I kept

82
00:07:47.066 --> 00:07:52.153
hammering until his cries stopped and his body fell limp to the ground. The master was dead

83
00:07:52.154 --> 00:07:56.074
and Mina was safe at last! When our ship docked in London, Mina was there to greet

84
00:07:56.075 --> 00:08:02.391
us with a smile on her face and a bouquet of flowers. "Such brave men!" she shouted,

85
00:08:02.392 --> 00:08:14.344
and then in my ear she whispered, "It’s too bad nobody else will ever know how

86
00:08:14.345 --> 00:08:18.066
brave you really are. My wonderful, strong Jonathan." I was happy that my adventure was finally over.

